<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d11" for="edge" attr.name="type" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d10" for="edge" attr.name="seq" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d9" for="edge" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d8" for="edge" attr.name="flow_id" attr.type="long" />
  <key id="d7" for="node" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d6" for="node" attr.name="service" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="node" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="graph" attr.name="graph_usable" attr.type="boolean" />
  <key id="d3" for="graph" attr.name="categories" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d2" for="graph" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="graph" attr.name="link" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="graph" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="directed">
    <node id="0">
      <data key="d5">NHS Digital Internal Teams</data>
      <data key="d6">UserCompanyAnalyst</data>
      <data key="d7">Internal NHS Digital teams (three user figures fused) who log in to look at and analyse data.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1">
      <data key="d5">EC2 Public Gateway (Guacamole)</data>
      <data key="d6">EC2</data>
      <data key="d7">Public gateway on the left of the dotted line. Users log into Guacamole here and land in a sandbox where they can analyse data but cannot get it out of the system.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2">
      <data key="d5">Active Directory</data>
      <data key="d6">DirectoryService</data>
      <data key="d7">Users authenticate via directory services so their identity is known. The user's role is also used by the data processing tools (Apache Ranger) so users only see the data they are meant to see.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3">
      <data key="d5">EC2 (Sandbox)</data>
      <data key="d6">EC2</data>
      <data key="d7">EC2 instance on the secure side of the dotted line, with an arrow to S3. Associated with moving existing datasets, converted to Parquet, into S3.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="4">
      <data key="d5">S3 Data Store</data>
      <data key="d6">S3</data>
      <data key="d7">Stores existing datasets converted to Parquet format. Confidential data, always encrypted at rest and in transit.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5">
      <data key="d5">EMR</data>
      <data key="d6">EMR</data>
      <data key="d7">Runs the analytics jobs and provides a consistent compute layer for the data. Reads the data from S3. Chosen over Cloudera and on-prem options for flexibility and scale. Jobs that took hours now take minutes or seconds. Supports tooling such as RStudio, JupyterHub and Hue.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="6">
      <data key="d5">KMS</data>
      <data key="d6">KMS</data>
      <data key="d7">Provides the key used to encrypt the data. Everything is encrypted in transit and at rest, including any other information in the system.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7">
      <data key="d5">Amazon RDS</data>
      <data key="d6">RDS</data>
      <data key="d7">Database in the secure environment with an arrow drawn from KMS. Its role is not described in the audio beyond other information in the system also being encrypted.</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="0" target="1" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Internal users log into the public gateway (Guacamole) to reach the sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="2" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Users are authenticated via directory services; their role determines data access (Apache Ranger).</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">Existing datasets are converted to Parquet format and put into S3.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="6" id="0">
      <data key="d8">2</data>
      <data key="d9">S3 uses a KMS key to encrypt the data (at rest and in transit).</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">1</data>
      <data key="d9">Arrow drawn from EMR to S3; per the audio, EMR reads the data from S3 to run analytics jobs.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6" target="7" id="0">
      <data key="d8">2</data>
      <data key="d9">Arrow drawn from KMS to RDS; any other information in the system is also encrypted.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <data key="d0">NHS Digital - Data Access Environment on AWS</data>
    <data key="d1">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SSWwnNVYi_Q</data>
    <data key="d2">Secure data access environment for NHS Digital internal teams, moving away from legacy systems. A public gateway (Guacamole on EC2) gives users access to a sandbox where they can analyse data but cannot extract it. Users authenticate via directory services; Apache Ranger enforces fine-grained access. Data is stored in S3 in Parquet format, encrypted with KMS at rest and in transit. EMR runs the analytics jobs; jobs that took hours now take minutes or seconds. Tooling includes RStudio, JupyterHub and Hue, with an aspiration towards machine learning.</data>
    <data key="d3">Analytics, Big Data, Security, Healthcare</data>
    <data key="d4">True</data>
  </graph>
</graphml>
